{
  "area": "ui-minimap",
  "description": "The minimap view-model (Features WV1, P2.core; catalog ui-minimap): the marker table, the live-feed fold, the projection onto a square map, and each marker type's tone and size. Runner: src/ui/hud-corpus.ts. Ops project {worldSize, position, sizePx, northYaw?, mirrored?} -> {x, y} (with northYaw the map is north up, east right: contract projectionNorthUp, P2.core-north; mirrored: true puts east left, contract projectionMirrored); toneFor {type} -> {tone}; sizeFor {type} -> {size}; session runs steps on a new MinimapModel(worldSize?) — {setWorldSize}, {add:marker}, {remove:id} -> {removed}, {clear:true}, {ingest:feed}, {setVisible} — and pins every result, worldSize, visible, markerCount, markers (insertion order), player, and with placed {sizePx, scale?, theme?, northYaw?, mirrored?} the placed list ({id, offsetX, offsetY, size, color, tone}; theme is role -> colour as data, and with no theme a marker with no colour of its own has color null). Every case is {name, op, input, expected}; numbers compare within tolerance, everything else exactly, object key sets included (a key TypeScript leaves undefined is absent). A non-finite number is written as null in an input. Regenerate with npm run hud-corpora; npm run hud-corpora:check fails on any difference.",
  "version": 1,
  "sources": [
    "Rules moved from babylon packages/babylon/src/engine/game-engine/ui/minimap-model.ts (babylon origin/main bfcdeb2, 279 lines) into core src/ui/minimap-model.ts unchanged; placed() takes the theme as an argument instead of defaulting to Babylon's uiTheme().",
    "Inputs are synthetic."
  ],
  "tolerance": 1e-9,
  "contract": {
    "markerTypes": [
      "player",
      "settlement",
      "npc",
      "quest",
      "quest_objective",
      "building",
      "exclamation",
      "question",
      "discovery"
    ],
    "tones": {
      "player": "accent",
      "settlement": "warning",
      "npc": "success",
      "quest": "quest",
      "quest_objective": "quest",
      "building": "text_disabled",
      "exclamation": "quest",
      "question": "quest",
      "discovery": "success"
    },
    "unknownTypeTone": "text_primary",
    "sizesPx": {
      "player": 6,
      "settlement": 8,
      "npc": 4,
      "quest": 7,
      "quest_objective": 5,
      "building": 3,
      "exclamation": 14,
      "question": 11,
      "discovery": 6
    },
    "unknownTypeSizePx": 4,
    "defaultWorldSize": 1024,
    "feedOwnedIds": "^(player|settlement_|npc_|quest_|objective_|item_|board_)",
    "feedIdPrefixes": {
      "playerPosition": "player",
      "settlements": "settlement_",
      "npcPositions": "npc_",
      "questMarkers": "quest_",
      "questObjectiveMarkers": "objective_",
      "questItemMarkers": "item_",
      "noticeBoards": "board_"
    },
    "projection": "x = ((p.x + w/2) / w) * size - size/2; y = ((p.z + w/2) / w) * size - size/2",
    "projectionNote": "projection is Babylon's rule, used when no northYaw is given; under the default north it draws north DOWN and so mirrors the world. Every engine binds projectionNorthUp",
    "projectionNorthUp": "with northYaw n (the world's, from worldNorth): k = size / w; east = (cos n, -sin n), north = (sin n, cos n); x = (p.x * east.x + p.z * east.z) * k; y = -(p.x * north.x + p.z * north.z) * k (north up, east right)",
    "projectionMirrored": "a mirrored level (the compass contract's mirroredLevel) passes mirrored: true with its northYaw: x is negated (north up, east LEFT, as the level shows it from above); y is unchanged. mirrored without a northYaw throws"
  },
  "cases": [
